      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/for_the_first_time_freshwater_crabs_from_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>For the first time ever, a species of large freshwater crab from Paraguay has been imported. The animals have a shell width of about 5-8 cm. Together with the legs these crabs are larger than a man's hand. They most probably belong to the species Trichodactylus kensleyi. The generic name means \"hairy finger\". The hairs on the lower segments of the legs are clearly visible in the pictures.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/for_the_first_time_freshwater_crabs_from_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>Crabs are very entertaining animals in the aquarium. They seem to be quite intelligent and display a great number of interesting behaviours. However, one must keep in mind that crabs are also great destructors. They tend to try any inhabitant of their tank – plants as well as animals – to see if it is edible. And these crabs are very pugnacious towards conspecifics.</p>"
    }
  ],
